### Pruebas manuales de POST /capital-payments (extensión REST Client de VS Code). Datos ficticios.
### Antes: crea dos tarjetas, un préstamo y una cuenta (cards.http, loans.http, accounts.http) y una
### compra con la primera tarjeta (expenses.http, caso 2, con fecha 2026-03-12). Cambia los ids:
@host = http://localhost:3001
@token = pega-aqui-el-accessToken-de-auth.http
@cardId = 1
@otherCardId = 2
@loanId = 3
@accountId = 4
@purchaseId = 1

### 1. Abono a una tarjeta, sin compra (el motor lo reparte por mayor tasa) -> 201 { "id": ... }
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": {{cardId}}, "date": "2026-03-25", "amountCents": 20000000 }

### 2. Abono a una compra de esa tarjeta, reduciendo la cuota -> 201
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": {{cardId}},
  "date": "2026-03-25",
  "amountCents": 20000000,
  "expenseId": {{purchaseId}},
  "mode": "reduce_payment"
}

### 3. Abono el mismo día de la compra -> 201
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": {{cardId}},
  "date": "2026-03-12",
  "amountCents": 20000000,
  "expenseId": {{purchaseId}}
}

### 4. Abono antes de la compra -> 400 "es antes de la compra"
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": {{cardId}},
  "date": "2026-03-11",
  "amountCents": 20000000,
  "expenseId": {{purchaseId}}
}

### 5. Compra de otra tarjeta -> 400
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": {{otherCardId}},
  "date": "2026-03-25",
  "amountCents": 20000000,
  "expenseId": {{purchaseId}}
}

### 6. Abono a un préstamo -> 201
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": {{loanId}}, "date": "2026-04-15", "amountCents": 200000000 }

### 7. Abono a un préstamo apuntando a una compra -> 400
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": {{loanId}},
  "date": "2026-04-15",
  "amountCents": 200000000,
  "expenseId": {{purchaseId}}
}

### 8. Abono a una cuenta -> 400
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": {{accountId}}, "date": "2026-03-25", "amountCents": 20000000 }

### 9. Producto que no existe -> 400 (el mensaje trae el id)
POST {{host}}/capital-payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 999, "date": "2026-03-25", "amountCents": 20000000 }
